-- title:
--   Reduced rings: √(a)∩√Ann(a)=0
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a reduced commutative ring (a ring in which the only nilpotent element is $0$) and let $a \in S$. Write $(a)$ for the ideal `Ideal.span {a}` generated by $a$, and $\operatorname{Ann}(a)$ for its annihilator as a submodule of $S$, i.e. the ideal of those $r \in S$ with $r \cdot (a) = 0$, equivalently $ra = 0$. For an ideal $I$, its radical consists of the $x$ with $x^n \in I$ for some $n$. The theorem asserts two statements simultaneously. First, the intersection of the two ideals $\sqrt{(a)}$ and $\sqrt{\operatorname{Ann}(a)}$ is the zero ideal $\bot$. Second, for every $s \in S$, if $a s$ lies in $\sqrt{\operatorname{Ann}(a)}$ then $s$ itself lies in $\sqrt{\operatorname{Ann}(a)}$; that is, multiplication by $a$ is injective on $S/\sqrt{\operatorname{Ann}(a)}$, so the image of $a$ is a non-zero-divisor there (or zero only when $s$ is).
--
--   This is the elementary commutative-algebra statement underlying the decomposition of the spectrum of a reduced ring into the closed subschemes cut out by $\sqrt{(a)}$ and $\sqrt{\operatorname{Ann}(a)}$, which meet in the empty scheme; in the present development it is used as the ring-theoretic input to [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.exists_smul_eq_nMap_of_nMap_eq_smul_of_isReduced`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.exists_smul_eq_nMap_of_nMap_eq_smul_of_isReduced).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_radical_span_inf_radical_annihilator_eq_bot_of_isReduced.lean

